To the Privacy / Data Protection team at {broker},

I am a California consumer submitting a verifiable request to delete my personal information and to opt out of its sale and sharing.

{scope}

{property_note}

Please delete all records matching ANY of the following identifiers — every record, not only the most recent or primary one:

{identifiers}

I am requesting that you:
  1. Delete all personal information you have collected about me, from {broker} and every property listed above, and direct your service providers and contractors to do the same (§ 1798.105(c)).
  2. Stop selling or sharing my personal information, and do not sell or share it in the future (§ 1798.120).
  3. Limit any use of my sensitive personal information to what § 1798.121 permits.
  4. Do not re-collect or re-list my information from other sources after this request.
  5. Confirm in writing, to the sending email address, once this is done, and tell me which records, if any, you did not delete and the legal reason.

{law}

If you need more to verify this request, reply to this email and I will provide what is reasonably necessary. Please do not require me to create an account (§ 1798.130(a)(2)) or to send a government ID or full date of birth.

{reference}

Thank you.

Sincerely,
{full_name}
